    "def-expectation-of-a-nonnegative-or-integrable-random-variable": {
      "id": "def-expectation-of-a-nonnegative-or-integrable-random-variable",
      "path": "items/def-expectation-of-a-nonnegative-or-integrable-random-variable.md",
      "status": "published",
      "domain": "mathematics",
      "kind": "definition",
      "exact_statement": "Let $(\\Omega,\\mathcal F,\\mathbb P)$ be a probability space.\n\n- If $X:\\Omega\\to[0,+\\infty]$ is measurable, its **expectation** is the\n  extended-valued integral\n  $$\\mathbb E[X]:=\\int_\\Omega X\\,d\\mathbb P\\in[0,+\\infty].$$\n- If $X:\\Omega\\to\\mathbb R$ or $X:\\Omega\\to\\mathbb C$ is integrable in the sense\n  of [[def-integrable-real-and-complex-functions-and-their-integrals]], its\n  **expectation** is again\n  $$\\mathbb E[X]:=\\int_\\Omega X\\,d\\mathbb P,$$\n  now a finite real or complex number.\n\nFor an integrable real random variable,\n$$\\mathbb E[X]=\\mathbb E[X^+]-\\mathbb E[X^-],$$\nwhere $X^+$ and $X^-$ are its positive and negative parts.",
      "sha256": "6a564c6ba82a58c9886f9dfffd23f5ea8029ecf28e033895cd20654d26108f09",
      "reading_status": "status/statement extracted; actual proof-reading extent belongs to specialist supplier record",
      "consumers": [
        "lem-qft-example-covariant-estimate-errors"
      ],
      "home_kind": "canonical-root-item",
      "original_page_homes": [
        {
