    "thm-riesz-representation-for-hilbert-space": {
      "id": "thm-riesz-representation-for-hilbert-space",
      "path": "items/thm-riesz-representation-for-hilbert-space.md",
      "status": "published",
      "domain": "mathematics",
      "kind": "theorem",
      "exact_statement": "Assume the Axiom of Countable Choice. Let $H$ be a real or complex Hilbert space and let $f$ be a bounded linear functional on $H$ ([[def-dual-space-of-a-normed-space]]). Then there is a unique $y\\in H$ with\n\n$$f(x)=\\langle x,y\\rangle\\qquad\\text{for every }x\\in H,$$\n\nand $\\|f\\|=\\|y\\|$, where $\\|f\\|$ is the dual norm ([[def-operator-norm]]). Under the first-variable-linear convention the representing vector depends conjugate-linearly and isometrically on $f$: if $f_i$ is represented by $y_i$ and $a,b$ are scalars, then $af_1+bf_2$ is represented by $\\overline a\\,y_1+\\overline b\\,y_2$.",
      "sha256": "0655811a363020d7b0df4d6ebbbc7ebb437adb0f4e098b7fb96959d3dc98c7c1",
      "reading_status": "status/statement extracted; actual proof-reading extent belongs to specialist supplier record",
      "consumers": [
        "lem-qft-polynomial-positive-compact-resolvent"
      ],
      "home_kind": "canonical-root-item",
      "original_page_homes": [
        {
          "path": "library/functional-analysis/hilbert-space-geometry-and-riesz-representation.md",
          "page": "hilbert-space-geometry-and-riesz-representation",
          "is_B": false,
          "status": "published"
        }
      ]
    },
    "thm-spectral-theorem-for-compact-self-adjoint-operators": {
      "id": "thm-spectral-theorem-for-compact-self-adjoint-operators",
      "path": "items/thm-spectral-theorem-for-compact-self-adjoint-operators.md",
      "status": "published",
      "domain": "mathematics",
      "kind": "theorem",
      "exact_statement": "Assume the Axiom of Countable Choice ([[def-countable-choice]]). Let $H$ be a\nreal or complex Hilbert space ([[def-hilbert-space]]) and let\n$T\\in\\mathcal B(H)$ be a compact self-adjoint operator\n([[def-compact-linear-operator]],\n[[def-self-adjoint-positive-unitary-and-normal-operator]],\n[[def-bounded-linear-operator]]). Let\n\n$$\\Sigma:=\\{\\lambda:\\lambda\\ \\text{is an eigenvalue of}\\ T,\\ \\lambda\\ne0\\}$$\n\nbe its set of nonzero eigenvalues\n([[def-eigenvalue-eigenvector-eigenspace-and-spectrum]]), with eigenspaces\n$E_\\lambda=\\ker(T-\\lambda I)$ for $\\lambda\\in\\Sigma$. Then:\n\n1. $\\Sigma$ is a finite or countably infinite set of **real** numbers, each\n   eigenvalue has finite multiplicity in the sense $\\dim E_\\lambda<+\\infty$, and\n   for every real $\\varepsilon>0$ there are only finitely many\n   $\\lambda\\in\\Sigma$ with $|\\lambda|\\ge\\varepsilon$; in particular every point\n   of $\\mathbb F\\setminus\\{0\\}$ has a neighbourhood containing only finitely\n   many elements of $\\Sigma$, so the only possible accumulation point of\n   $\\Sigma$ is $0$;\n2. the closed linear span $M$ of $\\bigcup_{\\lambda\\in\\Sigma}E_\\lambda$ satisfies\n   $$M=(\\ker T)^\\perp=\\overline{\\operatorname{ran}T}$$\n   ([[def-orthogonality-and-orthogonal-complement]]), and $H=M\\oplus M^\\perp$\n   with $M^\\perp\\subseteq\\ker T$;\n3. for every $x\\in H$ the finite-subset net of $\\sum_{\\lambda\\in\\Sigma}\\lambda P_\\lambda x$\n   over the orthogonal projections $P_\\lambda$ onto $E_\\lambda$ converges in\n   norm and\n   $$Tx=\\sum_{\\lambda\\in\\Sigma}\\lambda P_\\lambda x ;$$\n4. if in addition $H$ is a complex Hilbert space, then the nonzero spectrum\n   agrees with the nonzero eigenvalues,\n   $$\\sigma(T)\\cap\\{\\mu\\in\\mathbb C:\\mu\\ne0\\}=\\Sigma .$$\n\nNo Hilbert basis of $\\ker T$ is selected anywhere: only the orthonormal bases of\nthe finite-dimensional eigenspaces $E_\\lambda$, $\\lambda\\ne0$, are used.",
      "sha256": "6759cb2f44a85e0a6031d727311d37fc2743fa3baff8496084f299290005db72",
      "reading_status": "status/statement extracted; actual proof-reading extent belongs to specialist supplier record",
      "consumers": [
        "thm-qft-self-adjoint-regulated-interaction"
      ],
      "home_kind": "canonical-root-item",
      "original_page_homes": [
        {
          "path": "library/functional-analysis/compact-self-adjoint-hilbert-schmidt-and-trace-class-operators.md",
          "page": "compact-self-adjoint-hilbert-schmidt-and-trace-class-operators",
          "is_B": false,
          "status": "published"
        }
      ]
    },
    "lem-nuclear-series-characterizes-trace-norm": {
      "id": "lem-nuclear-series-characterizes-trace-norm",
      "path": "items/lem-nuclear-series-characterizes-trace-norm.md",
      "status": "published",
      "domain": "mathematics",
      "kind": "lemma",
      "exact_statement": "Assume the Axiom of Countable Choice ([[def-countable-choice]]). Let $H$ and $K$\nbe Hilbert spaces over the same real or complex scalar field and let $T\\in\\mathcal B(H,K)$ be compact\n([[def-compact-linear-operator]]). Then $T$ is trace class\n([[def-trace-class-operator]]) if and only if there are families\n$(u_j)_{j\\ge1}$ in $H$ and $(v_j)_{j\\ge1}$ in $K$, indexed by the positive\nintegers, with\n$$\\sum_{j\\ge1}\\|u_j\\|\\,\\|v_j\\|<+\\infty$$\nsuch that the zero-based sequence of finite-rank operators defined by $R_0=0$\nand\n$$R_m:=\\sum_{j=1}^{m}\\langle\\cdot,u_j\\rangle v_j\\qquad(m\\ge1)$$\nconverges to $T$ in operator norm ([[def-operator-norm]],\n[[def-metric-convergence]]).  Here the displayed scalar series is, under the\nlibrary convention, the series of the sequence\n$(\\|u_{m+1}\\|\\,\\|v_{m+1}\\|)_{m\\in\\mathbb N}$. In that case\n$$\\|T\\|_1=\\inf\\Bigl\\{\\sum_{j\\ge1}\\|u_j\\|\\,\\|v_j\\|:\\ R_m\\to T\\ \\text{in operator norm}\\Bigr\\},$$\nthe infimum being over all such **nuclear representations** of $T$, with the\nsame zero-based shift understood in every displayed sum, and the\ninfimum is attained: using its positive-integer index set and padding finite rank by zeros,\nthe singular-value series\n$T=\\sum_{j\\in J}s_j\\langle\\cdot,e_j\\rangle f_j$ is a nuclear representation with\nsum $\\|T\\|_1$.",
      "sha256": "57d9d23f78c960c08e891779a8bc313b97c9dab4157cb95befb09cc4c04b43ee",
      "reading_status": "status/statement extracted; actual proof-reading extent belongs to specialist supplier record",
      "consumers": [
        "thm-qft-regulated-gibbs-trace"
      ],
      "home_kind": "canonical-root-item",
      "original_page_homes": [
        {
          "path": "library/functional-analysis/compact-self-adjoint-hilbert-schmidt-and-trace-class-operators.md",
          "page": "compact-self-adjoint-hilbert-schmidt-and-trace-class-operators",
          "is_B": false,
          "status": "published"
        }
      ]
    },
    "thm-trace-of-a-positive-operator-is-the-sum-of-its-eigenvalues": {
      "id": "thm-trace-of-a-positive-operator-is-the-sum-of-its-eigenvalues",
      "path": "items/thm-trace-of-a-positive-operator-is-the-sum-of-its-eigenvalues.md",
      "status": "published",
      "domain": "mathematics",
      "kind": "theorem",
      "exact_statement": "Assume the Axiom of Countable Choice ([[def-countable-choice]]). Let $H$ be a\nreal or complex Hilbert space ([[def-hilbert-space]]) and let\n$T\\in\\mathcal B(H)$ be a **self-adjoint positive** trace-class operator\n([[def-self-adjoint-positive-unitary-and-normal-operator]],\n[[def-trace-class-operator]]), so that $\\langle Tx,x\\rangle\\ge0$ for every\n$x\\in H$. Let $\\lambda_1\\ge\\lambda_2\\ge\\cdots>0$ be the positive eigenvalues of\n$T$ listed with multiplicity\n([[def-eigenvalue-eigenvector-eigenspace-and-spectrum]]) and let\n$(s_n(T))_{n\\ge1}$ be the zero-padded singular-value sequence\n([[def-absolute-value-and-singular-values-of-a-compact-operator]]). Then\n$s_n(T)=\\lambda_n$ for every $n$, and\n$$\\operatorname{tr}(T)=\\sum_{n\\ge1}\\lambda_n=\\|T\\|_1 ,$$\nwhere the sum is over the positive eigenvalues with multiplicity and the\nequalities are also valid in the finite-rank case (then $\\lambda_n:=0$ for\n$n$ beyond the rank). This is the positive compact self-adjoint case only; it is\n**not** Lidskii's theorem for arbitrary trace-class operators, which is not\nclaimed here.",
      "sha256": "85c3861b7bb3f38a1418351c99bd464c5be4034780b1ec1d07fe1895027b425b",
      "reading_status": "status/statement extracted; actual proof-reading extent belongs to specialist supplier record",
      "consumers": [
        "thm-qft-regulated-gibbs-trace"
      ],
      "home_kind": "canonical-root-item",
      "original_page_homes": [
        {
          "path": "library/functional-analysis/compact-self-adjoint-hilbert-schmidt-and-trace-class-operators.md",
          "page": "compact-self-adjoint-hilbert-schmidt-and-trace-class-operators",
          "is_B": false,
