        }
      ]
    },
    "thm-tensor-product-distributions-and-iterated-pairings": {
      "id": "thm-tensor-product-distributions-and-iterated-pairings",
      "path": "items/thm-tensor-product-distributions-and-iterated-pairings.md",
      "status": "published",
      "domain": "mathematics",
      "kind": "theorem",
      "exact_statement": "For $u\\in\\mathcal D'(U)$ and $v\\in\\mathcal D'(V)$ the tensor candidate is a distribution on $U\\times V$, uniquely determined by $(u\\otimes v)(\\varphi\\otimes\\psi)=u(\\varphi)v(\\psi)$. Its two iterated pairing orders agree, and $\\operatorname{supp}(u\\otimes v)=\\operatorname{supp}u\\times\\operatorname{supp}v$. Three-factor pairings associate. Moreover $\\partial_x^\\alpha(u\\otimes v)=(\\partial^\\alpha u)\\otimes v$ and $\\partial_y^\\beta(u\\otimes v)=u\\otimes(\\partial^\\beta v)$. All claims hold in ZF.",
      "sha256": "8419ec7aa88effcfe8eb4ed0a8acf757fca4d543b22b17dad45d5806e9c51a24",
      "reading_status": "status/statement extracted; actual proof-reading extent belongs to specialist supplier record",
      "consumers": [
        "thm-qft-regular-wick-star-associativity"
      ],
      "home_kind": "canonical-root-item",
      "original_page_homes": [
        {
          "path": "library/functional-analysis/distributions-test-functions-and-differentiation.md",
          "page": "distributions-test-functions-and-differentiation",
          "is_B": false,
          "status": "published"
        }
      ]
    },
    "lem-distribution-pairing-with-smooth-parameter-families": {
      "id": "lem-distribution-pairing-with-smooth-parameter-families",
      "path": "items/lem-distribution-pairing-with-smooth-parameter-families.md",
      "status": "published",
      "domain": "mathematics",
      "kind": "lemma",
      "exact_statement": "Let $r,n\\ge1$ be integers, let $X\\subseteq\\mathbb R^r$ and $Y\\subseteq\\mathbb R^n$ be open, let $u\\in\\mathcal D'(Y)$, and let $F\\in C^\\infty(X\\times Y;\\mathbb C)$. Suppose that for each compact $H\\subseteq X$ there is compact $K\\subseteq Y$ with $\\operatorname{supp}_y F(x,\\cdot)\\subseteq K$ for every $x\\in H$. Then $a(x)=u(F(x,\\cdot))$ is smooth and $\\partial_x^\\alpha a(x)=u(\\partial_x^\\alpha F(x,\\cdot))$.\n\nAssume Countable Choice for the following integral clause. For every compact measurable $E\\subseteq X$, the function $G(y)=\\int_E F(x,y)\\,dx$ is a test in $\\mathcal D(Y)$, its $y$ derivatives pass under the integral, and $u(G)=\\int_E u(F(x,\\cdot))\\,dx$. Integrals here are Lebesgue integrals. The smoothness and differentiation claims hold in ZF; Countable Choice supplies Lebesgue measure for the integral clause. Neither clause uses tensor products or distributional mollification.",
      "sha256": "b6a2a63f5cf968d8877824f0470c982a4920299a391827a39fa7fc50dbe00cb4",
      "reading_status": "status/statement extracted; actual proof-reading extent belongs to specialist supplier record",
      "consumers": [
        "thm-qft-regular-wick-star-associativity"
      ],
      "home_kind": "canonical-root-item",
      "original_page_homes": [
        {
          "path": "library/functional-analysis/distributions-test-functions-and-differentiation.md",
          "page": "distributions-test-functions-and-differentiation",
          "is_B": false,
          "status": "published"
        }
      ]
    },
    "thm-baire-category-for-complete-metric-spaces": {
      "id": "thm-baire-category-for-complete-metric-spaces",
      "path": "items/thm-baire-category-for-complete-metric-spaces.md",
      "status": "published",
      "domain": "mathematics",
      "kind": "theorem",
      "exact_statement": "Assume the Axiom of Dependent Choice ($\\mathrm{DC}$). If a nonempty metric space $X$ is complete, then it is not the union of a sequence of closed sets each having empty interior. Equivalently, the intersection of countably many open dense subsets of $X$ is dense.",
      "sha256": "f53fe77e2f3a9eb12d4fa968920237be9b0b9eebc4b262df8a48332e41680346",
      "reading_status": "status/statement extracted; actual proof-reading extent belongs to specialist supplier record",
      "consumers": [
        "lem-qft-test-frechet-uniform-scaling-order"
      ],
      "home_kind": "canonical-root-item",
      "original_page_homes": [
        {
          "path": "library/real-analysis/approximation-and-compactness-in-ck.md",
          "page": "approximation-and-compactness-in-ck",
          "is_B": false,
          "status": "published"
        }
      ]
    },
    "thm-distributions-supported-at-one-point": {
      "id": "thm-distributions-supported-at-one-point",
      "path": "items/thm-distributions-supported-at-one-point.md",
      "status": "published",
      "domain": "mathematics",
      "kind": "theorem",
      "exact_statement": "For $a\\in\\Omega$ and $u\\in\\mathcal D'(\\Omega)$, $\\operatorname{supp}u\\subseteq\\{a\\}$ if and only if\n$$u=\\sum_{|\\alpha|\\le m}c_\\alpha\\partial^\\alpha\\delta_a$$\nfor some finite $m\\ge0$ and complex coefficients. The coefficients, with absent higher terms interpreted as zero, are unique. A nonzero such combination has support exactly $\\{a\\}$; the zero combination has empty support. This holds in ZF.",
      "sha256": "ebc9723feb448ccc4358f3e971cc445dea045f929d6c26344a3aced1a134e529",
      "reading_status": "status/statement extracted; actual proof-reading extent belongs to specialist supplier record",
      "consumers": [
        "prop-qft-local-counterterm-jet-classification"
      ],
      "home_kind": "canonical-root-item",
      "original_page_homes": [
        {
          "path": "library/functional-analysis/distributions-test-functions-and-differentiation.md",
          "page": "distributions-test-functions-and-differentiation",
          "is_B": false,
          "status": "published"
        }
      ]
    },
    "thm-fourier-basis-and-parseval-on-the-n-torus": {
      "id": "thm-fourier-basis-and-parseval-on-the-n-torus",
      "path": "items/thm-fourier-basis-and-parseval-on-the-n-torus.md",
      "status": "published",
      "domain": "mathematics",
      "kind": "theorem",
      "exact_statement": "Assume the Axiom of Countable Choice ([[def-countable-choice]]). Let $n\\ge1$\nand let $e_k(x)=\\exp(2\\pi i\\,k\\cdot x)$, $k\\in\\mathbb Z^n$, be the coordinate\ncharacters on $\\mathbb T^n$\n([[def-the-one-dimensional-torus-and-normalized-haar-integral]],\n[[def-fourier-coefficients-and-trigonometric-polynomials]]). Then:\n\n1. $(e_k)_{k\\in\\mathbb Z^n}$ is an orthonormal family in the complex Hilbert\n   space $L^2(\\mathbb T^n)$;\n2. it is an orthonormal basis: its closed linear span is $L^2(\\mathbb T^n)$;\n3. consequently the Fourier expansion\n   $f=\\sum_{k\\in\\mathbb Z^n}\\widehat f(k)e_k$ and Parseval's identity\n   $$\\|f\\|_2^2=\\sum_{k\\in\\mathbb Z^n}|\\widehat f(k)|^2,\\qquad \\langle f,g\\rangle=\\sum_{k\\in\\mathbb Z^n}\\widehat f(k)\\overline{\\widehat g(k)}$$\n   hold for all $f,g\\in L^2(\\mathbb T^n)$, in the finite-subset-net sense; and\n4. the Fourier coefficient map is a surjective linear isometry of\n   $L^2(\\mathbb T^n)$ onto $\\ell^2(\\mathbb Z^n,\\mathbb C)$.\n\nNo Hilbert tensor-product identification is used anywhere.",
      "sha256": "6d017415a6b810647e7c94b874eeaf15f46699e548ad6957fc16aad60600d968",
      "reading_status": "status/statement extracted; actual proof-reading extent belongs to specialist supplier record",
      "consumers": [
        "lem-qft-qed-coulomb-constraint",
        "def-qft-compact-lattice-gauge-data"
      ],
      "home_kind": "canonical-root-item",
      "original_page_homes": [
        {
          "path": "library/functional-analysis/orthonormal-bases-parseval-and-fourier-series.md",
          "page": "orthonormal-bases-parseval-and-fourier-series",
          "is_B": false,
          "status": "published"
        }
      ]
    },
    "thm-minus-laplacian-of-the-fundamental-solution-is-dirac": {
      "id": "thm-minus-laplacian-of-the-fundamental-solution-is-dirac",
      "path": "items/thm-minus-laplacian-of-the-fundamental-solution-is-dirac.md",
      "status": "published",
      "domain": "mathematics",
      "kind": "theorem",
      "exact_statement": "Assume Countable Choice and let $n\\ge2$. The locally integrable kernel $\\Phi$ of [[def-laplace-fundamental-solution-with-positive-minus-laplacian-sign]] defines a regular distribution $T_\\Phi\\in\\mathcal D'(\\mathbb R^n)$ and satisfies $-\\Delta T_\\Phi=\\delta_0$. For every $y\\in\\mathbb R^n$, the regular distribution associated with $x\\mapsto\\Phi(x-y)$ satisfies $-\\Delta_x T_{\\Phi(\\cdot-y)}=\\delta_y$.",
      "sha256": "8ebacd84f806e3a3c9f1217b326d1e892f5e9d658b1cc2d5987ee11a786dea5c",
      "reading_status": "status/statement extracted; actual proof-reading extent belongs to specialist supplier record",
      "consumers": [
        "cex-qft-qed-coulomb-potential-locality"
      ],
      "home_kind": "canonical-root-item",
      "original_page_homes": [
